{"repositoryId":646213203,"availability":"available","full":"flomesh-io/fsm","name":"fsm","description":"Lightweight service mesh for Kubernetes East-West and North-South traffic management, uses eBPF for layer4  and pipy proxy for layer7 traffic management, support multi cluster network. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":77,"forks":15,"created":"2023-05-27T16:44:59Z","updated":"2026-08-22T12:15:31Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://flomesh.io","topics":["ebpf","gateway-api","ingress-controller","kubernetes","load-balancer","multi-cluster","service-mesh","service-mesh-interface","sidecar"],"demo":"https://fsm-docs.flomesh.io/docs/getting_started/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.281Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.281Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.281Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.281Z","stars":77,"forks":15}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Flomesh Service Mesh (FSM) inherits a portion of the archived OSM code and introduces the following enhancements while maintaining compatibility with OSM:","Flomesh Pipy is a programmable network proxy that provides a high-performance, low-latency, and secure way to route traffic between services.","FSM is dedicated to providing a holistic, high-performance, and user-friendly suite of traffic management and service governance capabilities for microservices operating on the Kubernetes platform. By harnessing the combined strengths of FSM and Pipy, we present a dynamic and versatile service mesh solution that empowers Kubernetes-based environments."],"features":["FSM utilizes Flomesh Pipy proxy as a replacement for OSM's Envoy proxy. This enables FSM to achieve lightweight control and data planes, optimizing CPU and memory resources effectively.","Implemented traffic interception using eBPF-based technology instead of iptables-based traffic interception.","FSM offers comprehensive north-south traffic management capabilities, including Ingress and Gateway APIs.","Additionally, it facilitates seamless interconnectivity among multiple clusters and incorporates service discovery functionality.","Easily and transparently configure traffic shifting for deployments"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flomesh-io/fsm/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cc62c58de1ae654fa0ef4ec9dada053862a96300457c9b1aea3f86700350c8d9","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.425Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.425Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The Flomesh Service Mesh (FSM) inherits a portion of the archived OSM code and introduces the following enhancements while maintaining compatibility with OSM:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flomesh-io/fsm/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"cc62c58de1ae654fa0ef4ec9dada053862a96300457c9b1aea3f86700350c8d9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flomesh-io/fsm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.426Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-22T12:15:31Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flomesh-io/fsm/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:37.426Z","hash":"cc62c58de1ae654fa0ef4ec9dada053862a96300457c9b1aea3f86700350c8d9","originalBytes":11647,"storedBytes":11647,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["fsm","install","service","mesh","flomesh","guide","traffic","code","development","documentation","sidecar","support","version","control","kubernetes","license","proxy","smi","supported","using","community","docs","management","pipy","project","shell","start","cluster","comments","conduct","configure","demo","demonstration","design","features","gatewayapi","get","github","osm","overview","policies","prerequisites","quick","services","specification","usage","v1alpha2","v1alpha4","access","application","between","bin","binary","bookstore","brew","capabilities","cli","conduct.md","configured","contents","contri